  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "Rust returns ordinary/pair slots in tab-list order, with split members in pane order and a reachable pin anchor chosen in pane order. Inputs contain only indices and UI IDs.",
    "Rust also returns original-pin wrapper visibility. Native adapters instantiate the slots, insert a pair at its returned pin anchor and apply visibility without selecting pair membership or an anchor themselves.",
    "The shared browser regression opens two real pins at different folder depths, verifies B/A pane order and nested anchor, swaps to A/B and the outer anchor, swaps while the parent folder is collapsed, switches workspaces with the nested folder collapsed, then unsplits and restores both original pins.",
    "The cached plan is reused for metadata-only updates. Existing scene title/paint-ownership and large warm-sidebar cache-invariant regressions pass.",
    "Swipe previews consume the same cached tab/pin plan; pair selection and hidden-pin substitution no longer depend on native View visibility or an independent membership loop.",
    "Rust tests cover sparse tab indices, reverse pane order, one/two pinned members, collapsed-folder anchors, unreachable pins, missing/identical split members, duplicate tab indices and empty inputs.",
    "The full functional matrix retains native input/drag/scroll, folders and failed writes, workspace animation/swipes, sessions, palettes and settings."
  ],
  "manual_observations": [
    "The signed app displayed the original 24-tab demo, Unicode split pair and folder/pin tree.",
    "The native Split View menu action Move Right swapped the real pages and the Metal sidebar tiles in the same order; screenshot and accessibility tree agreed.",
    "The opposite menu action restored the original pane/tile order. The original demo session and expanded folder were retained and the prototype was closed.",
    "The normal browser app/profile was not used."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Application commands still own actual split sessions and WebContents; Rust plans UI representation only.",
    "Native View containers, hierarchy mutations, viewport/clipping, event/focus/accessibility and menu adapters remain.",
    "Swipe preview painting and its pair geometry remain native; this milestone shares grouping/visibility policy and does not establish pixel-level parity of every animated pinned-pair snapshot.",
    "Split pane headers/divider, outer sidebar controls, palettes/forms and full IME/VoiceOver coverage still require migration and verification.",
    "Functional elapsed times and submitted GPU frames are not a controlled CPU/GPU/physical-presentation benchmark; no end-to-end speedup is asserted.",
    "No new third-party crate, library or binary framework was added."
  ]
